   "subject": "ggtree: add black outline/border in edges colored with continuous state transition",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear all,<div><br></div><div>I wonder if you can help me how to add add black outline/border in edges colored with continuous state transition. I have produced a figure similar to this one &quot;Figure 4.11: Continuous state transition in edges.&quot; available here <a href=\"https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter4.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter4.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482051387000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2T7vTTIYdu8nGKNrHyzwMl\">https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter4.html</a></div><div><br></div><div>But I&#39;d like to add a thin black border in all tree branches, just like the argument outline=TRUE as available in phytools. I think ggtree would largely improve the presentation of the phylogeny with the possibility of adding an outline, particularly when yellow-colored branches are displayed.</div><div><br></div><div>I hope Guangchuang or anybody here would have a solution for this.</div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div><br></div><div>Domingos Cardoso</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "EywAlRCHAAAJ",
   "from": "Leonardo Borges",
   "author": "5980888bc7285774",
   "date": "2020-05-08T18:09:56Z",
   "subject": "Re: ggtree: add black outline/border in edges colored with continuous state transition",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Domingos,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">You could try to emulate edge outlines by placing a the tree with black and slightly thicker branches below your tree. <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">As ggtree works with layers, it should work. However, I could not find a way to overlay trees with different aesthetics... If you manage to do so, please share the solution with us.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Cheers,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:small\">Leo Borges<br clear=\"all\"></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://aquitemcaqui.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://aquitemcaqui.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482051390000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1UbvriBmWg8WOtuFebZK1Z\">aquitemcaqui.com</a></div><div><br><br></div></div></div><br></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
